 n____\n\nRobin Coste Lewis is a writer and artist. Lewis won the National 
 Book Award for Voyage of the Sable Venus\, her first collection of poe
 try. The book was also a finalist for the Hurston/Wright Legacy Award and 
 the Los Angeles Times Book Award\, and it was named one of the best bo
 oks of the year by The New Yorker and The New York Times. Literary H
 ub named it one of the best books of the last twenty years. Lewis was th
 e first African-American to ever win the National Book Award in a debut\, 
 and the first woman to do so since 1974. Her second book\, To the Realiz
 ation of Perfect Helplessness\, was the winner of the PEN/Voelcker Award f
 or Poetry and the NAACP Image Award for Outstanding Literary Work in Poetr
 y. She is also the coauthor\, with Kevin Young\, of Robert Rauschenberg:
  Thirty-Four Illustrations for Dante’s Inferno\, published by the Muse
 um of Modern Art. Her latest book\, Archive of Desire\, was named by the
  Brooklyn Public Library as one of the best poetry collections of the year
 . The former poet laureate of Los Angeles\, Lewis holds a PhD in poetry an
 d visual studies from the University of Southern California\, an MFA in po
 etry from New York University\, an MTS in Sanskrit and comparative religio
